// A member's access state, independent of BusinessRole. ACTIVE is the only
// state that existed implicitly before Business v1 (every member always
// had full access). SUSPENDED is new: it represents a non-owner member
// whose access is currently disabled because the business no longer holds
// Business-tier entitlement (see src/plugins/tenant.ts's downgrade-sync
// logic) — the row and all historical data it's linked to are preserved,
// only authorization is affected. The owner's own membership is never
// SUSPENDED (see Business.ownerId's doc comment on the ownership
// invariant).
enum BusinessMemberStatus {
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
}

// Lifecycle of one team invitation. EXPIRED is computed at read/accept time
// from `expiresAt` rather than written by a background job — see
// TeamInvitation's doc comment — but is still a real status value so an
// invite that's found to be expired at accept time can be durably recorded
// as such (a claim-guard update, not a cron).
enum TeamInvitationStatus {
  PENDING
  ACCEPTED
  EXPIRED
  REVOKED
}

